<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bastar Dussehra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bastar Dussehra is a festival held each year in Jagdalpur and across the Bastar region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, lasting about 75 days. Unlike Dussehra elsewhere, it is devoted to the goddess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danteshwari">Danteshwari</a> and the local deities of Bastar's villages rather than to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a>. Its rituals, including the pulling of a great wooden <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a>, bind the former ruling family to the region's Adivasi communities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bastar-dussehra.jpg" alt="Bastar Dussehra" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sushil.skk · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bastar_Dusshera_Unexplored_Bastar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
